            "title": "网球：我 和 朋友 Sophia",
            "material_text": "The friend I'd like to talk about is Sophia, who has been my best friend since I was around 8 years old. In fact, we ve known each other and have been teammates in the same tennis team for over a decade.I still remember the first time I met her — as two people who love sports, we met each other in tennis extracurricular classes.\n\nWhen we first started playing together, neither of us was very skilled. But my friend was always upbeat and supportive. She would often say that with practice, we'd surely improve. She'd analyze our games, point out areas where we could do better, not in a critical way but in a helpful,\nconstructive manner.\n\nLater, Sophia and I both managed to join the local tennis club and we talked about everything ranging from our practice to gossip and schoolwork. After that, we took part in many more competitions and won most of them. Gradually, we developed an unspoken understanding on the court — we could predict each other's moves without even talking. Our teamwork got stronger and stronger, and we became one of the best pairs in the local tennis community.\n\nTalking about why she is important to me, I mean, firstly, since we are in the same team, we definitely have…",
